A||||5||kneebarx||Steering Problem||||1||
Z||000000||kneebarx||11-08-2001||01:58 PM||||I have an extremely difficult time turning the wheel, especially when the car is idle.  Is this supposed to be like this in the fiero?  I saw some other guy driving the fiero and he had no trouble whatsoever.<P>I already tried doing searches on this topic, but I cant find anything on this type of problem.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hank is Here||11-08-2001||02:14 PM||||Welcome to the world of ARMstrong power steering!  The engine speed has nothing to do with the ease of steering since it isn't power.  I can tell you that there is a large difference between my 87 GT with 15" 205 tires and my 88 coupe with 14" 185 tires.  So the wider the tire you have the harder it is to turn.   <p>[This message has been edited by Hank is Here (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||peterh||11-08-2001||03:15 PM||||Check your tire pressure, make sure it is up to 32psi or whatever the normal tire pressure is. This makes a big difference for a non power steering car.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-08-2001||05:23 PM||||I've found it's <B>much</B> easier to turn the wheel when stopped once I removed my steering dampener.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-08-2001||08:08 PM||||Several things can be involved.<P>The steering damper could be bad. A good one shouldn't be very stiff at all. Most of the OE ones are shot now and either do nothing or bind.<P>The tire pressure is important. I believe all the OE tire sizes for Fiero are 30PSI. alternate sizes may need a couple PSI one way or the other. <P>Internal problem in the rack.<P>Bad alignment. (To much Caster.)<P>Big tires.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Kasdan||11-08-2001||09:22 PM||||I find it very easy to turm my wheel...i dont know wtf u people are talking about!  this is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> wait a sec....i have power steering, hehe!<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">               <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt motor with &gt;100 miles, Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
